    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\npagetitle: \"What 95% Confidence Means\"\n# Experimental animated explainer (inspired by Emil Hvitfeldt's tidy-animations).\n# One deck per animation: the animation code is in ci-anim.html next to this file.\n# Every number on the slide comes from the R chunk below.\nformat:\n  revealjs:\n    theme: [default, ../slides.scss]\n    width: 1280\n    height: 720\n    slide-number: false\n    hash-type: number\n    footer: \"Quantitative Methods I · Confidence intervals (L6 s8–s11) · experimental\"\n    include-after-body:\n      - ci-anim.html   # not ci.html: that name is the render output\nexecute:\n  echo: false\n---\n\n\n\n## What does \"95% confident\" mean? {.ci-slide}\n\n:::::: {.columns}\n::: {.column width=\"64%\"}\n```{=html}\n<svg id=\"ci-stage\" viewBox=\"0 0 820 580\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animated confidence intervals from repeated samples\"></svg>\n```\n:::\n\n::::: {.column width=\"36%\" .ci-captions}\n:::: {.ci-cap data-stage=\"0\"}\n**The population** (a teaching device)\n\n- Treat all 38,367 ESS respondents as the population\n- Satisfaction with democracy, 0 to 10\n- True mean: μ = 5.07\n- In real research μ is unknown\n::::\n\n:::: {.ci-cap data-stage=\"1\"}\n**One sample**, n = 100\n\n- $\\bar{x}$ = 4.97, $se = s / \\sqrt{n}$ = 0.25\n- 95% CI = $\\bar{x} \\pm 1.96 \\times se$\n- = [4.48, 5.46]: contains μ\n::::\n\n:::: {.ci-cap data-stage=\"2\"}\n**20 samples**\n\n- New sample, new mean, new interval\n- This time all 20 contain μ\n- Misses are rare: about 1 in 20\n::::\n\n:::: {.ci-cap data-stage=\"3\"}\n**100 samples**\n\n- 97 of 100 intervals contain μ (red = misses μ)\n- Over 1,000 samples: 94.5%\n- The 95% describes the method, not one interval\n::::\n\n:::: {.ci-cap data-stage=\"4\"}\n**Confidence level** (same sample)\n\n- 90%: $\\bar{x} \\pm 1.645 \\times se$\n- 95%: $\\bar{x} \\pm 1.96 \\times se$\n- 99%: $\\bar{x} \\pm 2.576 \\times se$\n- More confidence → wider interval\n::::\n\n:::: {.ci-cap data-stage=\"5\"}\n**Sample size**\n\n- n = 400: se = 0.13 (n = 100: 0.25)\n- 4 × n → se about halves\n- Larger sample → narrower interval\n::::\n\n:::: {.ci-cap data-stage=\"6\"}\n**Takeaway**\n\n::: {.example-interp}\n- About 95% of intervals built this way contain μ\n- One interval either contains μ or it does not\n:::\n\n::: {.interp-note}\nCourse wording (L6 s8): the \"value in population likely to be within these bounds\".\n:::\n::::\n:::::\n::::::\n\n<script>window.CI_DATA = {\"mu\":5.07329215210989,\"counts\":[2454,1432,2773,3891,3990,6434,4713,5420,4516,1920,824],\"means\":[4.97,4.78,5.01,5.24,5.02,5.16,5.15,5.21,5.18,5.47,5.48,4.94,4.75,5.26,4.96,5.32,4.66,5.05,5.06,5.09,5.11,4.9,5.35,5.39,5.28,4.78,5.2,4.59,4.96,5.3,4.89,5.09,4.69,4.95,4.87,5.34,5.03,5.37,5.15,5.04,5.25,5.01,4.87,5.51,5.12,4.83,5.26,5.21,4.98,5.13,5.18,4.84,5.17,5.14,5.04,4.79,5.59,5.31,4.78,4.72,4.68,4.95,4.71,5.3,5.09,4.97,5.1,5.1,4.75,5.04,4.55,4.9,4.92,4.93,4.92,4.74,5.11,5.18,4.99,4.87,4.92,5.09,4.87,4.6,4.95,5.18,5.08,5.03,5.03,5.2,4.74,4.9,4.66,5.05,5.36,5.05,4.66,5.17,4.91,4.4],\"lower\":[4.47835556742621,4.27655936764795,4.50894285654219,4.75020198102285,4.484875438271,4.67770658329397,4.65841871311434,4.72006335763147,4.67363888639259,4.94773811128511,4.96595720651355,4.43869122561766,4.24903579837165,4.78836424943382,4.45246010815091,4.82723214062571,4.14615351268569,4.56557515098476,4.54570061150133,4.5994301495385,4.61408052299111,4.4146748252434,4.85058737531279,4.93318028841906,4.80552605887353,4.2532068951158,4.67585058803753,4.03346611055479,4.41414933925259,4.79354693497748,4.37413739359509,4.57927808036866,4.1942370410013,4.43982542104677,4.36113534017364,4.89494793131771,4.54872544470359,4.88535091357798,4.63302531175808,4.54641385020168,4.77610298182159,4.47377797603054,4.38775888339395,5.03764488790827,4.60989768346602,4.31176584053113,4.7428414478317,4.70755079215442,4.48715339981579,4.62959381185749,4.67134508770879,4.35449895671554,4.65176584053113,4.63238365875497,4.50202597186342,4